SFS Lab solution
================

This directory contains a completed, AI-assisted solution, including optional
file-size, directory-growth, and Unix-unlink extensions.

From this directory:

    make
    make test                     # 12 correctness traces, then TSan if available
    make developer-test x-traces   # optional extensions
    make grade                    # optional calibrated performance benchmark

A correct coarse-lock implementation completes the basic exercise. This solution
retains fine-grained locking as a further optimization, not a new requirement.
The performance scale is local and is not an official CMU grading scale.

sfs-disk.c contains the implementation; sfs-api.h documents the API.
Run from this directory so the driver can find sfs-fsck and its source files.
Tests create private sfs-test.* directories; failed images remain for inspection.
make clean removes build products, not disk images.

The archive and PDF one directory above are the extension starter materials,
not this completed solution. Extract the archive elsewhere to start fresh.
For the simpler original-format starter, use https://github.com/LeeXSean/sfslab
on its main branch. Do not replace this solution's headers with the main-branch
headers: the optional empty-file encoding and unlink semantics are different.

Starter and test support: LeeXSean/sfslab, developer commit 8328843.
